#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:0 ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:2
msgid "FastAPI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:6
msgid "Layered configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:8
msgid ""
"Litestar uses a layered architecture. The parts used to group routes can "
"also be used to hierarchically organize an application. Settings and "
"configuration like dependencies, exception handlers, guards, middleware, "
"response cookies and headers, lifecycle hooks, OpenAPI configuration and "
"many more can be defined on any layer, and will be merged upon registration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:14
msgid "The layers in hierarchical order are"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:16
msgid "Application (``Litestar``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:17
msgid ""
"``Router`` / ``Controller`` (these are on the same level and can be "
"arbitrarily nested)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:18
msgid "Handler (``BaseRouteHandler``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:20
msgid ""
"When the same configuration is set on multiple layers, the value set closest "
"to the handler takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:25
msgid "Pydantic support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:27
msgid ""
"Litestar does support Pydantic, but other than FastAPI, it is mostly "
"agnostic about the modelling library you use. Litestar internally uses "
"`msgspec <https://msgspec.dev>`_, but also ships with support for Pydantic, "
"attrs and all builtin container types such as dataclasses or ``TypedDict``\\ "
"s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:32
msgid ""
"These, as well as ``msgspec``, are supported through its plugin system ( :"
"class:`~litestar.plugins.SerializationPlugin` and :class:`~litestar.plugins."
"OpenAPISchemaPlugin`) so it's easy to add first-class support for any "
"library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:39
msgid "Route handlers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:41
msgid ""
"Litestar does not expose decorators on the application or router. A route is "
"declared by a :doc:`route handler </usage/routing/handlers>` (function with "
"one of the method decorators, or a method on a :class:`Controller`) and then "
"registered on a :class:`Litestar` or :class:`Router` instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onboarding/fastapi.rst:52
msgid ""
"from fastapi import FastAPI\n"
"\n"
"app = FastAPI()\n"
"\n"
"@app.get(\"/\")\n"
"async def index() -> dict[str, str]: ..."
msgstr ""

